{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "stage": "A12",
  "title": "labels/comments/activity/appearance parity",
  "facts": [
    "A00/A10 roaming evidence includes board.snapshot appearance and the accepted board.appearance.put operation family.",
    "The frozen roaming/1 operation set does not establish label/comment mutation operations.",
    "A11 portable import preserves labels, cardLabels, comments, boardAppearanceSettings and activityEntries as opaque sections.",
    "Canonical A12 UTS 20260915T083858Z passed deterministic/frontend/offline Cargo lock+fetch gates and exposed Rust E0515 in parity portable-section materialization before native build."
  ],
  "inferences": [
    "Labels/comments must use an explicit local unsupported-sync ledger until a compatible roaming operation exists.",
    "Activity provenance should survive entity deletion and must not be fabricated for legacy history.",
    "payload.appearance is an Arch-native normalized event mapping over the proven board.appearance.put family, not a claim of unseen byte-identical Android event JSON."
  ],
  "proposals": [
    "Schema v6 materializes parity sections as first-class SQLite state behind domain/application repository contracts.",
    "Appearance reuses the A10 pending/outbox path while label/comment mutations stay outside pending_local_changes.",
    "Typed Tauri IPC exposes bounded parity operations without generic filesystem, keyring or network privilege."
  ],
  "unresolved": [
    "A compatible versioned cross-client wire contract for label/comment mutations remains future work.",
    "Exact legacy Android/web board.appearance.put payload bytes should be rechecked when original source archives are available.",
    "Canonical A12 Cargo/frontend/runtime UTS must be rerun after CORR-A12-001 before A13."
  ],
